const faq = [
["How much does a home battery cost in Indiana?", "EnergySage reports an average of $13,000 for a 13 kWh battery installed in Indiana before incentives, or about $1,000 per kWh, with a typical range of $11,050 to $14,950 (page updated November 15, 2026). EnergySage's separate first-half-2026 cost guide lists Indiana higher, at $1,333 per kWh, so get several quotes."],
["Are there battery rebates in Indiana?", "We haven't found one as of November 23, 2026. Indiana's Energy Saver Program (HEAR) is open to households under 150% of area median income, but its eligible list is heat pumps, heat pump water heaters and dryers, electric stoves, electrical panels, wiring, and insulation, not batteries. The federal 25D battery tax credit ended for installs completed after 12/31/2025."],
["How often does the power go out in Indiana?", "EIA reports the average Indiana customer was without power for 374 minutes (about 6.2 hours) in 2025 including major events, versus 262.6 minutes for the U.S. as a whole. Without major events it was 123.2 minutes, across about 1.4 interruptions a year."],
